<title>JAPAN: Japan April imported vehicle sales down 36.8% y/y.</title>
<headline>Japan April imported vehicle sales down 36.8% y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of imported vehicles in Japan fell 36.8 percent in April from a year earlier to 20,869 units, the Japan Automobile Importers Association (JAIA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It was the first decline in four months on a year-on-year basis, it said.  </p>
<p> Cars total		     18,980  down 38.4 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc	  12,154  down 45.8 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc	  6,826  down 18.4 percent</p>
<p> Trucks total		    1,889  down 16.2 percent</p>
<p> Buses			     nil  vs two</p>
<p>Exporting countries and selected makers' car sales in Japan in April, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> German total		    9,696  down 29.2 percent</p>
<p>  Volkswagen Audi Group	3,565  down 13.0 percent</p>
<p>  -Volkswagen		    2,995  down  6.4 percent</p>
<p>  -Audi				570  down 36.5 percent</p>
<p>  Mercedes-Benz		  2,368  down 34.5 percent</p>
<p>  Adam Opel			1,950  down 45.1 percent</p>
<p>  BMW				1,468  down 12.7 percent</p>
<p>  Ford-Werke AG		    194  down 61.4 percent</p>
<p>  Porsche			    140  down 40.7 percent</p>
<p> United States total	   4,972  down 47.0 percent</p>
<p>  Honda USA			2,331  down 32.3 percent</p>
<p>  General Motors		 1,018  down 40.9 percent</p>
<p>  Chrysler			   673  down 44.2 percent</p>
<p>  Ford Motor			 377  down 73.2 percent</p>
<p>  Toyota			     212  down 86.1 percent</p>
<p> Britain total		   1,903  down 26.6 percent</p>
<p>  Rover group		    1,577  down 29.3 percent</p>
<p>  Jaguar			     163  down 36.3 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan				94  up  623.1 percent</p>
<p> Sweden total		    1,019  down 61.3 percent</p>
<p>  Volvo				976  down 61.7 percent</p>
<p>  Saab				  43  down 51.1 percent</p>
<p> France total			540  down 48.5 percent</p>
<p>  Peugeot Citroen		  436  down 43.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Peugeot			  288  down 37.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Citroen			  148  down 51.6 percent</p>
<p>  Renault			    104  down 62.7 percent</p>
<p> Italy total			 537  down 13.4 percent</p>
<p>  Fiat group			 528  down  9.9 percent</p>
<p> Spain total			 150  down 74.7 percent</p>
<p>  Nissan			     150  down 74.7 percent</p>
<p> Netherlands			  92  vs  nil</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			  92  vs  nil</p>
<p> Australia			    21  down 85.2 percent</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi			  21  down 85.2 percent</p>
<p>General Motors' April car sales included 419 Cavaliers sold by Toyota, down 49.0 percent from a year earlier. The April total included 271 Nissan AD Van commercial vehicles made in Mexico, against five the year before.</p>
<p>Of the April total, sales of vehicles produced by overseas units of Japanese makers totalled 3,190, down 44.7 percent from a year earlier.</p>
